This was created for but then abandoned by Adam, re-promised to Abraham and Moses, glimpsed by Ezekiel as the present reality,

322
00:40:22,680 --> 00:40:26,680
when things seemed darkest to his people and most broken.

323
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:35,680
The cure was instantiated through Christ and his sacrificial gift, and it seemed consummated here in John's vision.

324
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:41,680
In this vision, God isn't saying anything new, I think someone during this series said.

325
00:40:41,680 --> 00:40:44,680
He's saying the same thing that he said over and over and over.

326
00:40:44,680 --> 00:40:48,680
Jesus taught us to ask for this daily.

327
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:54,680
He said, "You should pray our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name."

328
00:40:54,680 --> 00:41:00,680
We were just told that the one sitting on the throne high and lifted up in heaven has said that we will be his sons and have inheritance.

329
00:41:00,680 --> 00:41:03,680
He is our Father, our holy Father in heaven.

330
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:06,680
Hallowed be thy name, that means holy is your name.

331
00:41:06,680 --> 00:41:08,680
Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name.

332
00:41:08,680 --> 00:41:10,680
Thy kingdom come, thy will be done.

333
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:12,680
That is what this is picturing.

334
00:41:12,680 --> 00:41:16,680
His kingdom finally coming and his will done in all things.

335
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:20,680
No evil ever enters the gate, there's never night, there's never death, the sea is gone.

336
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:24,680
Forgive us our debts as we forgive our debtors.

337
00:41:24,680 --> 00:41:26,680
Give us this day our daily bread, right?

338
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:28,680
That means no scarcity in this new place.

339
00:41:28,680 --> 00:41:30,680
Forgive us our debts as we forgive our debtors.

340
00:41:30,680 --> 00:41:35,680
That is us imbibing the water of life and then returning it to others.

341
00:41:35,680 --> 00:41:37,680
It flows through us.

342
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:42,680
And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil.

343
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:45,680
He just said in this kingdom, there's no more any curse, there's no more sin.

344
00:41:45,680 --> 00:41:49,680
This is the picture of life in the holy city.

345
00:41:49,680 --> 00:41:54,680
For yours is the kingdom and the power and the glory forever and ever.

346
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:55,680
Amen.

347
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:56,680
So be it.

348
00:41:57,680 --> 00:42:01,680
He is sitting there in power and glory forever in this kingdom.

349
00:42:01,680 --> 00:42:11,680
This, which is on the screen, the Lord's Prayer, is a prayer invoking the end of Revelation.

350
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:13,680
This is what we're to pray for daily.

351
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:15,680
This is our focus.

352
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:18,680
So to end our series on Revelation, I'd like to do two things.

353
00:42:18,680 --> 00:42:23,680
First, I'd like us to all stand and pray the Lord's Prayer together in a way that we've never prayed it before.

354
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:28,680
Every time you pray this, you should see his promise from the end of Revelation.

355
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:34,680
And then the musicians are going to lead us in a closing song of holiness, okay?

356
00:42:34,680 --> 00:42:40,680
Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name.

357
00:42:40,680 --> 00:42:45,680
Thy kingdom come, and thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

358
00:42:45,680 --> 00:42:51,680
Give us this day our daily bread, and forgive us our debts as we forgive our debtors.

359
00:42:52,680 --> 00:42:55,680
Lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil.

360
00:42:55,680 --> 00:43:01,680
For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, forever and ever. Amen.
